{"title":"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> be an integer, and consider a circle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> equally spaced points marked on it. Consider all labellings of these points with the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611d2aeec0d82dcfefaec28099aeed290bf52eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, ... , n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> such that each label is used exactly once; two such labellings are considered to be the same if one can be obtained from the other by a rotation of the circle. A labelling is called beautiful if, for any four labels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79aaead4a185db1b2c9c7ccf238bd329165edfc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b &lt; c &lt; d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/818091c444ab6197a968e0b76308f59b18927229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + d = b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />, the chord joining the points labelled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> does not intersect the chord joining the points labelled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of beautiful labelings, and let N be the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da659214bd3a4e758702acefdd7bb4a8fca5d64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c0321f7ee4a767381d7a5e571c765f535516d7a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(x, y) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/239a121b99b77b803b45983b56020afdc92a2abf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M = N + 1.\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO\" title=\"2013 IMO\">2013 IMO</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO\" title=\"2013 IMO\">2013 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232715\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 110/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1288/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 50/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2469/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.365      1 -total\n 52.02%    6.953      1 Template:IMO_box\n 46.95%    6.275      1 Template:Solution\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16373:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232715 and revision id 204561. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}